Here is a launchable Megatron-DeepSpeed MoE configuration for a ~1B dense-equivalent (activated-parameter) model — 8 experts per layer, top-2 routing, ~2.0B total / ~0.9B active params.

```json
{
  "framework": "megatron-deepspeed",
  "architecture": {
    "num_experts": 8,
    "top_k": 2,
    "hidden_size": 2048,
    "num_layers": 16,
    "capacity_factor": 1.25,
    "expert_ffn_size": 2048,
    "sequence_length": 2048,
    "vocab_size": 50304
  },
  "parallelism": {
    "data_parallel": 4,
    "expert_parallel": 2,
    "tensor_parallel": 1,
    "pipeline_parallel": 1,
    "world_size": 8
  },
  "batch_size": 1048576,
  "estimated_memory_gb": 36,
  "estimated_tokens_per_sec": 180000,
  "launch_notes": "Megatron-DeepSpeed MoE: each FFN replaced by 8 experts, top-2 gating, capacity factor 1.25 (drops ~15% tokens under imbalance; add router aux + z losses). Launched on 8xH100-80GB: deepspeed pretrain_gpt.py --model-parallel-size 1 --expert-parallel-size 2 --num-experts 8 --topk 2 --capacity-factor 1.25 --num-layers 16 --hidden-size 2048 --ffn-hidden-size 2048 --micro-batch-size 8 --global-batch-size 512 (512 seq x 2048 tok = 1.05M tok/step) --bf16 --recompute-activations. DP=4, EP=2 shards experts across 2 GPUs; attention/embedding replicated under DP, optimizer ZeRO-1 with fp32 AdamW (master ~14GB/GPU). Est. 36 GB/GPU incl. activations; ~180k tok/s (~45% MFU); all-to-all overhead scales with experts, so keep EP small relative to world size for a 2B-param model."
}
```

Rationale: hidden 2048 × 16 layers gives ~0.9B active params (attention + top-2 experts), ~2B total with 8 experts — a typical Mixtral-style 4:1 total-to-active ratio. top_k=2 with capacity 1.25 balances load and quality; EP=2/TP=1 suits a small model on 8 GPUs.